  "_commit": {
    "id": "847fc37dd8b70a61f7aafb7f6d6266031b720499",
    "author": "Patrick Aboyoun <aboyoun.patrick@gene.com>",
    "committer": "Patrick Aboyoun <aboyoun.patrick@gene.com>",
    "message": "feat: add st_join_table for sparse joins between two lazy spatial tables (0.99.8)\n\nst_intersects_table() only ever supported testing x against a single\nreference geometry -- its y goes through .geom_to_sql(), which has no\ncase for another lazy table -- so there was no way to get a sparse match\ntable between two out-of-core layers short of materializing the full\nattribute join via st_join(). This blocked spatialJoin(DuckDBDataFrame,\nDuckDBDataFrame) in BiocDuckDB, whose sparse=TRUE branch called\nst_intersects_table(x, y) and always errored with \"unsupported geometry\ntype: DuckDBDataFrame\" when both sides were out-of-core.\n\nAdded st_join_table(x, y, join = st_intersects, sparse = TRUE), modeled on\nthe existing st_join.DuckDBTable: same INNER JOIN ... ON <predicate>(...)\napproach and the same .st_predicate_sql_name() mapping to honor join=,\nbut projecting a sparse (id_x, id_y) row-pair table instead of full\nattributes.\n",
    "time": 1792512982
  },
